      "math_academy_id": "e-5841",
      "problem": "Find the range of the function $f(x)=\\dfrac{3}{4x-1}+2.$",
      "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{a}{bx+c} + d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\in (-\\infty, d)\\cup (d,\\infty).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d = 2.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y = 2,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\in (-\\infty, 2) \\cup (2, \\infty).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248368/assets/fb344a1c6613805bab7bcc04c8b711b5ba1c26eef36197c45b03205e2bc5dbc6.png)",
